A||||7||gabriel|| VATS &3800SC technical questions||||1||
Z||000000||gabriel||02-28-2001||08:42 AM||||Hi all.<P>  Hmmmm ...  I'm seeing a VATS issue in the 3800SC swap.<P>  Questions:<P>   If I can get the VATS module from the donor car, would that be easier than tricking up the existing system?<P>   What is the passkey box, anyway?<BR>  I'm not sure if the key still exists for the donor.<P>  Anyone else use the donor fuse/relay box?<P>  -Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||elfiero||02-28-2001||09:46 AM||||1.I use the VATS module from the donor car.<BR>2.if you can't find the original key for the<BR>module,go to a auto alarm installation store<BR>and buy a VATS resistor kit(20.00).this matches the value of the key-presto! it works<BR>3.passkey is a slightly different system,but<BR>the method of defeating it is the same.||||reg||6
Z||000002||gabriel||02-28-2001||10:25 AM||||Thanks elfiero!<P>  I just called the supplier & they can get the VAT & key & the tumbler if need be, But it's all very labor intensive. The VAT is hidden behind the dash & heater box setup to prevent jumpering the VAT.<P>  He said that I could use any GM VAT & then do the VATS resistor trick that you described.<P>  But there's one thing that's not clear to me.<P>  Since the Fiero doesn't even have a VAT or the tumbler setup in the column, would I just setup the VAT module anywhere & connect the VATS resistor kit to it?  Or is there more to this?<P>  Again, thanks!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||elfiero||02-28-2001||12:45 PM||||really its just 4 wires,power,ground,two wires to the ign. tumbler.I just tape it to<BR>the ECM with the resistor siliconed to the<BR>module and hooked to the tumbler wires.||||reg||6
Z||000004||terryk||02-28-2001||12:57 PM||||There are several solutions. What year is the ECM? You can do the resistor, a vats eliminator or change the code.<P><BR>Passkey comes in several flavors, each more complex. That's why the year is important to know.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrfixit58||02-28-2001||03:40 PM||||If you can fish the VATS modual and steering column wiring out of the donor car, the most trick thing to do is to re-install the tumbler into your steering column. It will requiring you to dismantle both columns. Do the donor first and and apply what you learn to install the system into your column. When completed, it'll look factory and add a little added theft protection.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||3
Z||000006||gabriel||02-28-2001||04:10 PM||||Thanks guys.<P>  Terry, the donor is an 97 Olds LSS complete, w/4T65E, harness, PCM, and everything else you had advised.<BR> I didn't know the OBY-II could be changed.<BR>What is a VATS eliminator?  Sounds elegant.<P>  Mrfixit 58, I like that solution as well, but ...<BR>  The problem is that this donor is in another state, & I would have to pay this guy by the hour to take out the dash, heater, VAT, then take the tumbler out of the column.  That's  a lot of wasted money if I can go to a local boneyard & make another VAT work with silicone & resistors.<P>  I'm also beginning to see that the Fiero isn't going to stop many thieves without some help ...<P>  Again, thanks guys.  I believe that we have a fantastic repository of information on this forum.  <P>   Just doing everything by trial & error would take quite a while.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  -g||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||02-28-2001||11:20 PM||||Best thing to do is find a matching set in a local yard. dig that out and hook it up. That will give you all the pieces like that.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.franken.de/users/dagobah/luke/fieroidx.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.franken.de/users/dagobah/luke/fieroidx.html</A>  has an article on this. He's not had time to finish it yet but it should help. <P>also if you search the <A HREF="http://www.MotorAge.com" TARGET=_blank>www.MotorAge.com</A>  archives there's an article there with a bunch of stuff.<P>This is a feature I intend to add to my car in the not distant future. ||||reg||1
